/-!
# All-time confinement for the `μ > 0` passing guiding-centre fields of a pitch-angle cell

For every `λ = μB₀/E ∈ [1/8, 3/16]` the exact passing torus of `mu_family_torus` is a flow torus of
the `μ > 0` passing field `gcFieldMu (1/256) λ = B + ∇×(ρ(x) b)`, `ρ = ρ₀√(1 − λ|B|)`, with
`0.03 ≤ rt ≤ 0.255`, so it traps the field lines of that field and of the passing guiding-centre
velocity field `VmuF c (1/256) λ` (`mu_family_master`).

**The field in cylindrical form.** `B̃ = gcField(ρ₀ F(x))` pointwise with
`F = (1 − λ|B|/2)/√(1 − λ|B|)` (`gcFieldMu`), so its cylindrical components are those of
`gcField (rM λ R z φ)` (`cRTZ_gcFieldMu`), and the certified flow form `gcFlowMu` evaluates to
them on the torus (`eval_gcDM_ptC`, ...).

**The profile.** Star-shapedness and positive winding follow from the certificate for the
`μ = 0`, `ρ = 1/256` torus `K₀` (`gc_radial_ge`, `gc_winding_ge`) and the distance
`‖K(λ) − K₀‖ ≤ 1.85 × 10⁻³` in `u, z, ∂_θu, ∂_θz` on the strip `r_A` (`muOld_u`, ...), from the
low-resolution `λ`-family chain against the stored low-resolution `K₀` (`normLM_dUo`, ...) and the
old distances (`dist_u`, ...).

**Sanity.** `rM_zero`, `mu_family_lam_zero`: at `λ = 0` the field is the `μ = 0` field (`λ = 0`
lies outside this cell; these are checks of the definitions only).

Pitch cell `λ ∈ [1/8, 3/16]`: modules `RationalStellaratorGCMu3*`,
namespace `PlasmaLean.Design.RationalStellaratorGC.Mu3`; generated by
`scripts/gc_kam/lamcell` from the pipeline of the cell `[0, 1/16]`.
-/

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace

@[expose] public section
noncomputable section

